---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
import { breadcrumbs, graph, organization, website } from '../lib/schema';

const trail = [
	{ name: 'Home', path: '/' },
	{ name: 'Terms', path: '/terms' },
];
const jsonLd = graph(organization(), website(), breadcrumbs(trail));
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms"
	description="What using this site does and does not create, and the limits on everything published here."
	jsonLd={jsonLd}
	pageType="editorial"
>
	<PageHeader
		eyebrow="Terms and limitations"
		title="Research informs a decision. It is not the decision."
		lede="Reading this site does not create a broker relationship, does not bind coverage, and does not obligate any insurer."
		trail={trail}
	/>

	<section class="band band-tight">
		<div class="prose-shell prose">
			<h2>General information only</h2>
			<p>
				Everything published here is general educational information. It is not legal, tax, medical,
				engineering, appraisal, lending, investment, claims, or individualized insurance advice. It
				does not account for your circumstances, because it does not know them and does not ask.
			</p>

			<Callout tone="warn">
				<p>
					<strong>No coverage determination and no eligibility decision is made anywhere on this
					site.</strong> Only an authorized insurer or its representative can decide whether a risk
					is acceptable, what a policy covers, what it costs, and whether a specific claim is
					payable. Nothing here substitutes for that, and nothing here should be relied on as though
					it did.
				</p>
			</Callout>

			<h2>No relationship is created</h2>
			<p>
				Using this site does not create a broker, agent, fiduciary, or advisory relationship with
				{' '}{siteConfig.operator.legalName} dba {siteConfig.operator.dba}. A relationship begins only
				if you separately choose to engage the brokerage through its own disclosed intake, and it is
				governed by that engagement rather than by this site.
			</p>
			<p>
				Editorial review by a licensed person means that person checked the accuracy and the limits of
				the page. It does not mean they reviewed your situation, because they have not seen it.
			</p>

			<h2>Policy language</h2>
			<p>
				Statements about what a policy covers or excludes describe published forms, identified by form
				name and edition where possible. Your own policy is controlled by the exact form,
				endorsements, declarations, and state amendments attached to it, which may differ materially
				from anything described here. Read your own documents and ask your insurer to confirm.
			</p>

			<h2>Sources and accuracy</h2>
			<p>
				Every material claim is mapped to a source, and every source shows the date it was last
				checked. Public records, statutes, regulations, and published guidance change, sometimes
				without notice and sometimes retroactively. A page that was accurate on its review date may
				not be accurate today, which is why the date is shown on every page and why stale sources are
				flagged rather than hidden.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you find an error, <a href="/corrections">report it</a>. Corrections are published with the
				prior wording intact.
			</p>

			<h2>Tools</h2>
			<p>
				The tools organize information you enter. They do not submit anything to any insurer, do not
				accept documents, and do not produce a quote, a determination, or an eligibility result.
				Everything you type stays in your own browser. Output is a working document for your own use
				and for the conversation you choose to have next.
			</p>

			<h2>Outbound links</h2>
			<p>
				Source links open the publisher's own site. Those publishers are independent, their content is
				theirs, and their terms and privacy practices govern what happens once you arrive. A link is a
				citation, not an endorsement.
			</p>

			<h2>Intellectual property</h2>
			<p>
				Cited sources remain the property of their publishers and are linked rather than reproduced,
				beyond the short quotation needed to show what a source actually says. The original analysis,
				content model, interface, and methodology of this site belong to
				{' '}{siteConfig.operator.legalName}. Quotation with attribution and a link to the canonical
				URL is welcome, and is described in <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>. Republishing pages
				wholesale under another domain is not.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				These terms may change. Material changes will be dated. Continued use after a change means the
				current version applies.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`}>{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
